## 5️⃣  Using real vector tiles (`.pbf`)

Replace the **source definition** in the style with a **vector** source:

```json
{
  "type": "vector",
  "tiles": ["cache://tiles/{z}/{x}/{y}"],
  "minzoom": 0,
  "maxzoom": 14
}
```

And make sure you **store the raw PBF bytes** in IndexedDB:

```ts
// Example: fetch a vector tile from a public endpoint and cache it
async function cacheVectorTile(z: number, x: number, y: number) {
  const url = `https://tileserver.example.com/data/v3/${z}/${x}/${y}.pbf`;
  const resp = await fetch(url);
  if (!resp.ok) throw new Error(`Failed to fetch ${url}`);
  const arrayBuffer = await resp.arrayBuffer();
  await cache.put(z, x, y, new Uint8Array(arrayBuffer));
}
```

When the protocol handler returns the `ArrayBuffer`, MapLibre will automatically decode the protobuf and render the layers you defined in your style.

