## 4️⃣  Things to keep in mind

| Topic | Details |
|-------|---------|
| **Abort handling** | The `params.signal` passed to the protocol handler is the same `AbortSignal` that MapLibre uses for tile cancellation (e.g. when the user pans fast). Forward it to any `fetch` you do, as shown above. |
| **MIME type** | Vector tiles are `application/x-protobuf` (or `application/vnd.mapbox-vector-tile`). If you return a `Response` you can set `Content-Type`. Returning a raw `ArrayBuffer` works fine because MapLibre already knows it’s a vector tile from the source type. |
| **Cache size** | IndexedDB has a per‑origin quota (usually ~50 MiB, but browsers may allow more). You may want to implement an LRU eviction policy. The wrapper above is deliberately minimal; you can add a `lastAccessed` timestamp and prune old entries. |
| **Cross‑origin restrictions** | Because the tiles are read from IndexedDB, there is **no CORS** involved. The only network request is the
